---
import PublicLayout from '../layouts/PublicLayout.astro';
---

<PublicLayout
  title="Privacy Notice | St. Paul's Mission Hospital"
  description="How St. Paul's Mission Hospital collects, uses, and protects the personal data of job applicants, in accordance with the Kenya Data Protection Act, 2019."
  canonicalPath='/privacy'>
  <section class='border-b border-[var(--color-border-soft)]'>
    <div class='max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-10 pt-20 sm:pt-28 pb-12 sm:pb-16'>
      <p
        class='text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-[var(--color-brand)] mb-5'>
        Legal
      </p>
      <h1
        class='text-[2rem] sm:text-4xl font-black tracking-[-0.025em] leading-[1.1] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-6'>
        Privacy notice.
      </h1>
      <p class='text-[15px] text-gray-600 leading-[1.75]'>
        This notice explains how St. Paul's Mission Hospital collects, uses,
        stores, and protects personal data submitted through our recruitment
        portal, in accordance with the Kenya Data Protection Act, 2019.
      </p>
      <p class='text-[12px] text-gray-400 mt-4 italic'>
        Effective date: 1 January 2026 · Version 1.0
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class='bg-white'>
    <div class='max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-10 py-16 sm:py-20'>
      <div class='prose-legal'>
        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          The data controller is St. Paul's Mission Hospital, P.O. Box 426, Homa
          Bay, Kenya, a faith-based Level IV mission hospital owned by the
          Catholic Diocese of Homa Bay.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Data we collect</h2>
        <p>When you apply for a position through our portal, we collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your full name, email address, and phone number.</li>
          <li>Your CV or résumé and any additional documents you upload.</li>
          <li>Any cover letter or message you choose to provide.</li>
          <li>
            Your consent record (date and version of this notice you accepted).
          </li>
          <li>
            Basic technical information about your submission (date, time,
            source).
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          For volunteers and partnership enquiries, we collect the fields shown
          on the relevant forms — typically your contact details, location,
          areas of interest, and any message or proposal you submit.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Why we collect it</h2>
        <p>Your personal data is used solely for the following purposes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>To assess your suitability for the position you applied for.</li>
          <li>To communicate with you about your application.</li>
          <li>To comply with legal and regulatory requirements.</li>
          <li>To maintain records of our recruitment activity.</li>
          <li>
            For volunteer and partnership enquiries, to review and respond to
            your submission.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Lawful basis for processing</h2>
        <p>
          We process your personal data on the basis of your explicit consent,
          which you provide by ticking the consent box before submitting your
          application. You may withdraw consent at any time by contacting us,
          although this will not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out
          before withdrawal.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Who has access</h2>
        <p>Access to your personal data is strictly limited to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Authorised Human Resources staff of St. Paul's Mission Hospital.
          </li>
          <li>
            Hiring managers involved in the specific recruitment process, only
            for the role you applied for.
          </li>
          <li>
            Our infrastructure providers (Supabase for secure data storage,
            Resend for email delivery), under contracts that protect your data.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We never sell your personal data. We do not share it with third
          parties for marketing purposes.
        </p>

        <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We retain application data for a period of twelve (12) months from the
          date of submission for candidates who are not shortlisted, after which
          it is securely deleted. For candidates who progress through the
          recruitment process, and for any successful candidate, records are
          retained in accordance with applicable employment law and our internal
          retention policy.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may request earlier deletion of your data at any time (see section
          8).
        </p>

        <h2>7. How we protect it</h2>
        <p>We apply the following safeguards:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>All traffic to our portal is encrypted in transit via HTTPS.</li>
          <li>
            CVs and documents are stored in a private, access-controlled bucket.
            They are not publicly accessible.
          </li>
          <li>
            Only authorised HR staff can view applications, and every access is
            logged.
          </li>
          <li>
            Data is stored on infrastructure with strong physical and logical
            security controls.
          </li>
          <li>
            Staff who handle personal data receive confidentiality training.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under the Kenya Data Protection Act, 2019, you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Access the personal data we hold about you.</li>
          <li>Request correction of any inaccurate data.</li>
          <li>Request deletion of your data.</li>
          <li>Object to or restrict processing in certain circumstances.</li>
          <li>Withdraw consent at any time.</li>
          <li>
            Lodge a complaint with the Office of the Data Protection
            Commissioner (ODPC).
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, contact the Human Resources
          Department at
          <a href='mailto:info@spmh.co.ke'>info@spmh.co.ke</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Our careers portal does not use advertising cookies or third-party
          trackers. We use only the technical storage necessary for the portal
          to function and for you to submit an application securely.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Changes to this notice</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this notice periodically. When we do, we will revise the
          effective date at the top of the page. Significant changes will be
          communicated through the portal.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For questions about this notice or how we handle your personal data,
          contact:
        </p>
        <p class='contact-block'>
          Human Resources Department<br />
          St. Paul's Mission Hospital<br />
          P.O. Box 426, Homa Bay, Kenya<br />
          Email: <a href='mailto:info@spmh.co.ke'>info@spmh.co.ke</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PublicLayout>

<style>
  .prose-legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .prose-legal h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .prose-legal p {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #4b5563;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }
  .prose-legal ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }
  .prose-legal ul li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.35rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #4b5563;
  }
  .prose-legal ul li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.6rem;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--color-brand);
  }
  .prose-legal a {
    color: var(--color-brand);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .contact-block {
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--color-warm);
    border-radius: 12px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
</style>
